cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use neuro-convert in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "neuro-convert: streaming, verified conversion of neurophysiology recordings to NWB"
abstract: >-
  Converts neurophysiology recordings (TDT, SpikeGLX, Intan, Open Ephys, Blackrock, Neuralynx) to
  NWB 2.11, as a Zarr store or an HDF5 file, from a command line or a desktop app written in Rust.
  Recordings are streamed block by block, samples keep their stored integer type, and the written
  data is read back and compared with the source (xxh3-64 per block); each reader is compared value
  for value with a reference reader on public test data.
authors:
